          %h3#for_functors_preserving_filtered_colimits For functors preserving filtered colimits
          %p
            Returning now to existence of general coequalizers, here is a more difficult and arcane result given in
            %a{:href => "#BarrWells"} Toposes, Triples, and Theories
            (theorem 3.9, p. 267):
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a category with finite colimits, colimits of chains
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa \to C
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              an infinite cardinal), and equalizers of arbitrary sets of endomorphisms. If a monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T : C \to C
              preserves colimits of
              = succeed "-chains," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^T
              admits coequalizers.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_4 Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
